WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.380
Property managers need to know what's coming due,
and what's already late.

2
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.900
This calendar lists every recurring task by property,

3
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.570
with when it was last done and when it's next due.

4
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.120
Due dates follow the spec's rule:
when a month runs short,

5
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.120
the date lands on its last day.

6
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.150
August 31 plus six months is February 28.

7
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.200
Overdue work is flagged in red, most overdue first.

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.400
Filter by status, property or category,

9
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.420
and sort by urgency or name.

10
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.590
Mark a task done, and its next due date
moves forward from today.

11
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.940
Wrong one? Undo puts it back.

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.120
One addition: a 30-day look-ahead,

13
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.620
so vendors get booked before anything is late.

14
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.160
Built with React and TypeScript, 83 tests,

15
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.110
and a layout that works on phones.
